algorithms.pseudocode:
Algorithm: CertifyLorentzianCondition
Input:  Leaf Hessians H_1, ..., H_m in R^{n x n}
Output: Certified condition bound kappa, or FAIL

1. For each k = 1, ..., m:
   a. Compute eigenvalues lambda_1 >= ... >= lambda_n of H_k
   b. If #{i : lambda_i > 0} > 1, return FAIL
   c. Set g_k = min{|lambda_i| : lambda_i < 0}
   d. Set N_k = max{|lambda_i|}
2. Return kappa = max_k (N_k / g_k)

Complexity: O(m * n^3) for eigenvalue decomposition
